{\b About this software}\par
SabhaMujic is a music player for sabha volunteers. This setup installs:\par
\pard\li240\sa60 - the SabhaMujic Playback Service, a Windows service that runs as NT SERVICE\\SabhaMujic and starts automatically;\par
- the SabhaMujic desktop app, with a Start menu shortcut and an optional desktop shortcut;\par
- two Windows Firewall rules for the iPhone remote, inbound TCP 8443 and 8080, on Private networks only.\par
\pard\sa100 The music library, accounts and settings are stored in %ProgramData%\\SabhaMujic (usually C:\\ProgramData\\SabhaMujic). Uninstalling SabhaMujic keeps that folder. The setup guide (docs/SETUP.md) explains how to remove it completely.\par
{\b Third-party components}\par
SabhaMujic includes the following components. Each is used under its own license, shown in parentheses.\par
\pard\li240\sa60 - .NET runtime, ASP.NET Core, Windows Presentation Foundation, Microsoft.Extensions libraries and Microsoft.Data.Sqlite, by Microsoft (MIT)\par
- NAudio, by Mark Heath and contributors (MIT)\par
- StreamJsonRpc, Nerdbank.Streams, Microsoft.VisualStudio.Threading and Microsoft.VisualStudio.Validation, by Microsoft (MIT)\par
- MessagePack for C# (MIT), Nerdbank.MessagePack (MIT), PolyType (MIT) and Newtonsoft.Json (MIT)\par
- SignalR JavaScript client (@microsoft/signalr), by Microsoft (MIT)\par
- CommunityToolkit.Mvvm, by Microsoft and the .NET Foundation (MIT)\par
- QRCoder (MIT)\par
- Dapper (Apache License 2.0)\par
